<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fakhr al-Din Bahramshah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died c. 1225</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fakhr al-Din Bahramshah was the Mengujekid ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erzincan">Erzincan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kemah">Kemah</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> for about sixty years, from the 1160s until his death around 1225. A patron of learning, he received the dedication of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizami-ganjavi">Nizami</a>'s poem <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/makhzan-al-asrar">Makhzan al-Asrar</a>. He kept close ties with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> of Rum, who absorbed his family's lands soon after his death.</p></div>
